    "### Set comprehension\n",
    "\n",
    "**Takeaway:** `{x for x in seq}` removes duplicates.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Sets are unordered; the sorted-looking output is not guaranteed.\n",
    "- `set(duplicates)` does the same; `unique` is reused by the comprehension cell below.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "9c081b6c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "duplicates = [1,1,1,2,3,4,4,5,6,6,7]\n",
    "unique = {x for x in duplicates}\n",
    "print(unique)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md000003",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Generators\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interview answer:** a generator produces values lazily, one at a time, so it is memory-efficient for large data.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Function with `yield` = generator function; calling it returns a generator iterator.\n",
    "- `yield` returns a value and pauses until the next one is asked for.\n",
    "- ⚠️ Single-use. The `for` loop below calls `get_numbers()` again → a **new** generator, so it restarts at 1.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "599972c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "1\n",
      "2\n",
      "1\n",
      "2\n",
      "3\n",
      "4\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def get_numbers():\n",
    "    yield 1\n",
    "    yield 2\n",
    "    yield 3\n",
    "    yield 4\n",
    "numbers  = get_numbers()\n",
    "print(next(numbers))\n",
    "print(next(numbers))\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in get_numbers():\n",
    "    print(i)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md000004",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Generator expression\n",
    "\n",
    "- `( ... )` instead of `[ ... ]`; lazy, one value at a time. Official term: _generator expression_ (not \"generator comprehension\").\n",
    "- Printing shows only the object; consume with `next()`, `for`, `list()`, `sum()`.\n",
    "- `next` is a built-in **function**, not a keyword.\n",
    "- Here the `for` reuses the **same** generator, so it continues: `5 7 9`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "id": "a5303375",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Normal list using comprehension : [0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10]\n",
      "Generator : <generator object <genexpr> at 0x7eb2d44192f0>\n",
      "Yes this wont print anything other than the object reference... you have to use next keyword to print\n",
      "1\n",
      "3\n",
      "5 7 9 "
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "even_numbers = [i for i in range(0,11) if i%2==0]\n",
    "print(f\"Normal list using comprehension : {even_numbers}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "odd_numbers = (i for i in range(0,11) if i%2!=0)\n",
    "print(f\"Generator : {odd_numbers}\\n\"+\n",
    "      \"Yes this wont print anything other than the object reference... you have to use next keyword to print\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(next(odd_numbers))\n",
    "print(next(odd_numbers))\n",
    "for i in odd_numbers:\n",
    "    print(i, end = ' ')"
   ]
  },
