   "source": [
    "### `==` calls `__eq__`\n",
    "\n",
    "`a == b` → `type(a).__eq__(a, b)`\n",
    "\n",
    "- `NotImplemented` → try reflected `type(b).__eq__(b, a)`\n",
    "- Right operand is an overriding **subclass** → its method goes **first**\n",
    "- Both `NotImplemented` → falls back to identity, no error\n",
    "- Direct call skips this: `(5).__eq__(5.0)` is `NotImplemented`, but `5 == 5.0` is `True`\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "894faa04",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "True\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "a = 5\n",
    "b = 5\n",
    "print(a.__eq__(b))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md000007",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Access modifiers\n",
    "\n",
    "Python has no enforced private/protected; it runs on trust.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `_name` → \"internal, don't touch\" (convention). Still accessible. `import *` skips it unless listed in `__all__`.\n",
    "- `__name` → name mangling (next cell).\n"
   ]
  },
