    "### Polymorphism and method overriding\n",
    "\n",
    "**Takeaway:** same method call, different behaviour depending on the object's class.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Overriding: a child redefines a parent method; Python picks the child's version at runtime.\n",
    "- `Dog` has no `__init__`, so `Dog()` runs `Animal`'s constructor. `Cat` and `Husky` override `__init__` without `super().__init__()`, so `Animal`'s never runs for them.\n",
    "- `super().method()` inside an override would extend the parent's behaviour instead of replacing it.\n",
    "- No method overloading in Python; use default parameter values.\n",
    "- Only `Dog` is instantiated here; `Cat` and `Husky` are defined but unused.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
