    "### Dataclasses + lambda sort\n",
    "\n",
    "**Takeaway:** `@dataclass` generates `__init__`/`__repr__`/`__eq__` from the annotations; `asdict` turns an instance into a dict; `sort(key=lambda ...)` orders by a tuple key.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Closest Java match is a `record`, but a dataclass is **mutable** unless `@dataclass(frozen=True)`.\n",
    "- Annotations are hints only: `animal_weight: float` still accepts the int `200`.\n",
    "- `sort` is **stable** and in place. The 2nd sort decides the order; the 1st (by `cost`) only breaks ties between equal kind and weight, so here it changes nothing.\n",
    "- Key `(animal_kind, -animal_weight)` = kind ASC, weight DESC. Negating only works for numbers.\n",
    "- Output `['Tiger', 'Lion', 'Elephant']`: Carnivores first (heavier Tiger before Lion), then Herbivore.\n",
    "- Lambda 2: `max(zoo_dict, key=lambda x: x[\"cost\"])` returns the whole dict with the highest cost (Elephant).\n",
    "- Lambda 3: `check = lambda x: x%2==0`; `check(5)` → `False`. Prefer `def` when you name it (PEP 8).\n",
    "\n",
    "⚠️ `say_something` calls itself → `RecursionError` if ever called (never called here). It should `print` a string, not `self.say_something()`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7c303c62",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "['Tiger', 'Lion', 'Elephant']\n",
      "{'animal_name': 'Elephant', 'animal_kind': 'Herbivore', 'animal_weight': 800.5, 'cost': 100000.8, 'size_range': 'XXXL'}\n",
      "False\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#Dataclasses -> Similar to records in Java and asdict \n",
    "#Lambdas\n",
    "\n",
    "from dataclasses import dataclass, asdict\n",
    "\n",
    "@dataclass\n",
    "class Zoo:\n",
    "    animal_name: str\n",
    "    animal_kind: str\n",
    "    animal_weight: float\n",
    "    cost: float\n",
    "    size_range: str\n",
    "    \n",
    "z1 = Zoo(\"Lion\", \"Carnivore\", 200, 80000, 'L')\n",
    "z2 = Zoo(\"Tiger\", 'Carnivore', 250, 79999, 'L')\n",
    "z3 = Zoo('Elephant', 'Herbivore', 800.5, 100_000.80, 'XXXL')\n",
    "\n",
    "zoo_dict = [asdict(z) for z in [z1,z2,z3]]\n",
    "\n",
    "#--------------+-----------------+---------------+--------------#\n",
    "#Lambda 1\n",
    "zoo_dict.sort(key= lambda o : (o[\"cost\"])) # Sort by cost ASC\n",
    "zoo_dict.sort(key=lambda x : (x[\"animal_kind\"], -x[\"animal_weight\"])) # sort by animal_kind ASC, animal_weight DSC\n",
    "print([n[\"animal_name\"] for n in zoo_dict])\n",
    "\n",
    "#Lambda 2\n",
    "print(max(zoo_dict,key=lambda x : x[\"cost\"]))  # Using a lamdba in an Aggregate function\n",
    "\n",
    " #Lambda 3\n",
    "check = lambda x: x%2==0   \n",
    "print(check(5))"
   ]
  },
