    "### Quick review: mutability + lambda\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Lambda 3:** `check = lambda x: x%2==0` is an anonymous one-expression function; `check(5)` → `False`. Prefer `def` when you assign it to a name (PEP 8).\n",
    "- **Mutable:** list, dict, set. **Immutable:** tuple, str, int, float, frozenset. Only hashable (immutable) objects can be dict keys / set members.\n",
    "- **List vs generator:** list stores everything (fast re-use, more memory); generator is lazy and single-use.\n",
    "- **Interview traps from this notebook:** shallow vs deep copy, `==` vs `is`, `*args` tuple vs `**kwargs` dict, generator exhaustion, name mangling is not security.\n"
   ]
